From d914ed87c461f6fc3476bc46b7f157fbf6ca806d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fred Horch <fred.horch@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:37:54 -0400
Subject: Expand editor max column width from 65 to 80 characters

Omawrite previously clamped editorWidth to Math.round(writerFontMetrics.averageCharacterWidth * 65).
On modern widescreen displays, 65 characters feels overly narrow, leaving excessive
empty space on wide screens while wrapping lines sooner than standard 80-column limits.

Raising the ceiling to 80 characters increases line capacity while preserving
dynamic responsive shrinking on narrower windows (where width - 20 * avgCharWidth < 80 * avgCharWidth).

Retires when: upstream provides configurable column width or adopts 80 cols in pkgver > 0.5.0

(Patch carried in ~/pkgs by Fred's Omarchy workstation; registry: https://github.com/greenermoose/omarchy-fred-ecosystem)

AI-Tool: claude 2.1.274
AI-Model: Claude Opus 5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Main.qml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Main.qml b/src/Main.qml
index b7afe4d076efbdbb361a525726801b2201a762a5..82eed17794037eae9d80f21b6da5a759f2c09fa9 100644
--- a/src/Main.qml
+++ b/src/Main.qml
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ ApplicationWindow {
     readonly property real textScale: backend.textScale
     readonly property int editorFontPixelSize: scaledSize(20)
     readonly property int editorWidth: Math.min(
-        Math.round(writerFontMetrics.averageCharacterWidth * 65),
+        Math.round(writerFontMetrics.averageCharacterWidth * 80),
         Math.max(360, width - Math.round(writerFontMetrics.averageCharacterWidth * 20)))
     property bool closeConfirmed: false
     property bool searchOpen: false
